        "text": "Page: Buda Limestone. Sentence: The Buda Limestone is a geological formation in the High Plains and Trans-Pecos regions of West Texas whose strata date back to the Late Cretaceous.\nPage: High Plains (United States). Sentence: The southern region of the Western High Plains ecology region contains the geological formation known as Llano Estacado which can be seen from a short distance or from on satellite maps.\nPage: Woodbine Formation. Sentence: The Woodbine overlies the Maness Shale, Buda Limestone, or older rocks, and underlies the Eagle Ford Group or Austin Chalk.",
